 harbor:[FIC,['I count the boats at dawn,','the gulls, the gray, the slow tide.','You said you would come by morning.','It is evening now. I am still counting.']],
 garden:[FIC,['All summer the garden kept its rows in order,','the beans in line, the marigolds in rank.','But frost came in one night without a warning,','and now the rows are only lines of mud.']],
 market:[FIC,['The market hummed with bargains and bright cloth,','and children chased the dogs between the stalls.','Then the bell rang once, and every voice went quiet.']],
 free:[FIC,['The bus is late.','A woman folds her coat across her knees','and reads the sky.']],
